{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "arceme-datacubes",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "Multi-sensor Earth observation data cubes generated within the ARCEME project (Adaptation and Resilience to Climate Extremes and Multi-hazard Events). Each data cube covers a 10 \u00d7 10 km area centred on an extreme weather event site from the WOCAT / DHP database. Cubes integrate four satellite sources:\n\n  \u2022 Sentinel-2 L2A \u2013 13 multispectral bands + SCL scene classification\n    (10 m / 20 m / 60 m, resampled to 10 m)\n  \u2022 Sentinel-1 RTC \u2013 VV and VH SAR backscatter (10 m)\n  \u2022 Copernicus DEM GLO-30 \u2013 digital elevation model (30 m, resampled to 10 m)\n  \u2022 ESA WorldCover 2020 \u2013 land-cover map at 10 m\n\nThe temporal window spans 12 months before and after the recorded event date. Pixel resolution is 10 m; tile size is 1000 \u00d7 1000 pixels (10 \u00d7 10 km). Cloud masking is applied to Sentinel-2 data using the SEnSeIv2/SegFormerB2 model.\n",
